{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EVIDENCE for the criterion the completion verifier flagged unmet ('a test asserts _verifier_cfg resolves the standard class, exercised through its real callers at xcheck.py:198 and xcheck.py:336 rather than in isolation').\n\nThe verifier was RIGHT and I treated it as a genuine gap, not a documentation gap. Checked before acting: tests/unit/test_verifier_class.py had 4 tests, all of which call _verifier_cfg directly or go through completion._verifier_model_for_completion; and tests/unit/test_plan_review_xcheck.py does reach maybe_apply_contradiction / maybe_apply_comment_trail but only asserts DROP behaviour (which findings survive), never the model the sub-call runs under. Those two properties are independent: a caller passing plain cfg instead of _verifier_cfg(cfg) would leave Pass-2/Pass-4 on the frontier model while every isolated test stayed green — precisely the silent-inheritance defect 172e exists to remove.\n\nFIXED in commit f7613bde6, Gerrit change 1128 (test-only, no source change). Two tests drive the REAL entries with a recording runner that captures each RunRequest's config; both sub-calls build RunRequest(config=_verifier_cfg(cfg)), so the captured model IS what the verifier path runs under:\n  test_contradiction_xcheck_resolves_standard_through_its_real_caller\n  test_comment_trail_xcheck_resolves_standard_through_its_real_caller\n\nVACUOUS-PASS GUARDS, because both entries are inert by default: each test enables the specific config gate (contradiction_xcheck_active / comment_trail_xcheck_active), the comment-trail test supplies a non-empty ctx.state['comments'] (that entry returns early with no trail), and each test asserts the sub-call ACTUALLY RAN (rr.seen_models non-empty) before asserting what it ran on.\n\nTEETH VERIFIED, not assumed: mutating both call sites from config=vcfg to config=cfg turns both tests red with the leaked id in the message — 'contradiction xcheck ran on [anthropic:claude-opus-4-8]'. cfg.model is a provider-qualified frontier id in one test and a Bedrock frontier id in the other, so the assertion also covers the provider-qualified case the original equality heuristic missed.\n\nFiled as a follow-up commit rather than an amend of ef060e80d because that commit sits mid-stack and this environment has no interactive rebase. NOT closing 172e until 1128 is Verified +1: change 1119 is already +1, but 1119 is not the change that satisfies this criterion."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785523158839173001,"uuid":"2ff9162a-bfca-4e4a-8dfd-9f58f766f760"}